## Agentic Harness

Every instruction, skill, agent, and page lives once in the repository, and each coding assistant reaches it from its
own entry point. One copy keeps a single source of truth and spends fewer tokens. It also ships with the code, so a new
machine, a new tool, or a second developer starts with the same knowledge.

### File Layout

An assistant reads the files marked "Yes" before any task, and the others only when a task needs them.

<div align = "center">

| Path | Role | Always Read |
| :---: | --- | :---: |
| [AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md) | Guardrails, the registry of skills and agents, and the routing table | Yes |
| `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` | Shared skills | No |
| `.agents/agents/<role>.md` | Shared agent roles, with a name and a description as their only frontmatter | No |
| `docs/` | One page per topic | No |
| [CLAUDE.md](../CLAUDE.md) | Entry point of Claude Code: hands over to `AGENTS.md`, plus what only Claude Code needs | By its vendor |
| [GEMINI.md](../GEMINI.md) | Entry point of Gemini CLI and Antigravity | By its vendor |
| [copilot-instructions.md](../.github/copilot-instructions.md) | Entry point of GitHub Copilot | By its vendor |

</div>

### Vendor Files

What each vendor folder holds, because no other tool can use it:

<div align = "center">

| Vendor | Path | Role |
| :---: | :---: | --- |
| Claude Code | `.claude/skills/`, `.claude/agents/` | Pointer files to `.agents/`, with the frontmatter only Claude Code reads |
| {Vendor} | `{path}` | {What it does} |

</div>

### Adding A Skill Or An Agent

  1. Write it once, as `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` or `.agents/agents/<role>.md`. The folder or file name matches
     the frontmatter `name`, and no other `.md` file sits directly in either folder.
  2. Add its pointer file, `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` or `.claude/agents/<role>.md`, with the same name and
     description. Keys that only Claude Code understands go into the pointer.
  3. Add its row to the registry in `AGENTS.md`.

### Wiring A New Tool

  1. A tool that reads `AGENTS.md` needs no file. For one that does not, add its own entry point, under 15 lines, that
     hands over to `AGENTS.md`.
  2. Keep the settings, hooks, and commands of the tool in its own folder, and list them under **Vendor Files**.
  3. Never copy a rule, a skill, or a page into the folder of a tool. Point at the shared file.

</div>
